        "path": "_m/u/b/4/3/bosporan-kingdom-wp/hero.jpg",
        "filename": "Grave stele 03 pushkin.jpg",
        "caption": "Stele with two warriors of the Bosporan Kingdom. From Taman peninsula (Yubileynoe), Southern Russia, 3rd quarter of the 4th century BC. Marble, Pushkin museum\n\nThe marble relief was found in 1985. It is 1.88 m high, above 0.85 m and below 0.94 m wide. The plate is 0.25 m thick, the relief protruding 0.12 m. Also the whole surface of the plate is worked – the shield of the older warrior is reaching to the very margin of the stone. Two soldiers are represented, gazing each other. The bearded soldier has all attributes of a hoplite; the younger is only holding a spear.",
        "alt": "Stele with two warriors of the Bosporan Kingdom. From Taman peninsula (Yubileynoe), Southern Russia, 3rd quarter of the 4th century BC. Marble, Pushkin museum\n\nThe marble relief was found in 1985. It is 1.88 m high, above 0.85 m and below 0.94 m wide. The plate is 0.25 m thick, the relief protruding 0.12 m. Also the whole surface of the plate is worked – the shield of the older warrior is reaching to the very margin of the stone. Two soldiers are represented, gazing each other. The bearded soldier has all attributes of a hoplite; the younger is only holding a spear.",
